  },
  "description": "SADPUL crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C165 H226 Co4 Gd6 N6 O51 P6,9(C2 H3 N1),C1 H2 Cl2. From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd4 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd5 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd6 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Co1 (Co) has 4 O neighbors; Co2 (Co) has 4 O neighbors; Co3 (Co) has 5 O neighbors; Co4 (Co) has 5 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 10 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.111-3.952 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 90.75-111.92°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Co4Gd6(CarbpPO3)6(tBuCO2)14(tBuCO2H)(H2O)3]·9CH3CN·CH2Cl2. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 3 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 3 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)). Article name explicitly identifies Co(II), Gd(III).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
